From 3d48c0870e32751a8faf7b91e4699c292dbeff0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: g2code33 <g2code33@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:54:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix dark-mode select contrast app-wide, fix silent
 upload-save failures, default embedded browser to Google + add pin tabs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. Dark mode contrast:
   - Fixed a CSS bug where a large multi-line selector list (covering every
     tinted -50/-100/-200 background used for badges/alerts across the app)
     was missing commas between lines, so the whole rule compiled into one
     impossible selector that matched nothing — none of those tinted panels
     were ever actually remapped for dark mode, only the plain gray/slate
     ones were.
   - Added dark-mode remapping for the -700/-800/-900 text color tiers of
     every Tailwind color family (designed for contrast on a WHITE
     background, so they went dark-on-dark once the panel behind them went
     dark) and for plain black/gray-900/slate-900 text.
   - <select> elements specifically stayed native-white in dark mode on
     platforms (WebKitGTK/Linux) that paint the closed combobox chrome with
     the OS theme regardless of CSS background-color, while still honoring
     the CSS text color — producing near-invisible light-on-white text.
     Neutralized native appearance and drew a matching custom chevron so
     every <select> in the app (Search, Learning Objectives, Quiz, Notes,
     Settings, Material Library, ...) now actually uses our dark palette.

2. Upload / "No file is stored for this material": saveFile() caught and
   swallowed IndexedDB write failures, resolving as if the save had
   succeeded either way. Every upload path (FileUploader, manual
   add/edit-slide modals in StudyMaterials and CourseDetail, legacy bulk
   upload) created its material/slide record unconditionally afterwards, so
   a device with a failing/full IndexedDB produced normal-looking materials
   whose bytes were never actually saved — exactly the "No file is stored
   for this material" dead end reported from the reader, with no warning at
   upload time to explain why. saveFile() now reports success/failure via
   its return value, and every call site checks it: a failed save now shows
   a clear, immediate error and skips creating the broken record instead of
   silently going on to /read.

3. Embedded browser (SlideReader): default search engine changed from
   DuckDuckGo to Google, using the `igu=1` parameter that makes Google's own
   server omit the X-Frame-Options header that otherwise blocks it from
   being framed at all (DuckDuckGo remains available as one of the quick
   Study links). Added a per-tab pin: a small pin toggle on every open tab
   lets the user keep it around — pinned tabs sort to the front and persist
   across visits to the reader (saved to localStorage), independent of the
   fixed Wikipedia/PubMed/PubChem/DailyMed/Google/DuckDuckGo quick-link
   pills.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
